@* The frame of the Server sample (PkApp, PkModuleBoundary, PkRouteGuard) on WebAssembly. OnNavigateAsync loads the lazy module before the router matches the route (an in-app click reaches the router first;
   a router that cannot match reloads the page). The guard calls the same loader, which has it already. The boundary wraps the guard so a failed download shows Try again. *@
@inject PkLazyModuleLoader Loader

<PkApp>
    <PkModuleBoundary>
        <PkRouteGuard>
            <Router AppAssembly="typeof(Program).Assembly" AdditionalAssemblies="Loader.Assemblies" OnNavigateAsync="c => Loader.LoadForPathAsync(c.Path, c.CancellationToken)">
                <Found Context="routeData"><RouteView RouteData="routeData" /></Found>
                <NotFound><PkNotFoundPage /></NotFound>
            </Router>
        </PkRouteGuard>
    </PkModuleBoundary>
</PkApp>
